        {"after": "## 3. The Three Major Classes",
         "md": "**Deep dive — pigments classify the algae.** Algal classes are named by colour because colour is the visible summary of the pigment set: chlorophylls plus accessory pigments. Chlorophyceae (green) carry chlorophyll a and b like land plants — which is exactly why green algae are considered the ancestors of the plant kingdom. Phaeophyceae (brown) add fucoxanthin; Rhodophyceae (red) add r-phycoerythrin, which absorbs the blue-green light that penetrates deepest water — the reason red algae can live deeper than any other alga."},
